If sd(loss)/Ubar stays bounded below, the best-in-class competitor fluctuates at order Ubar/sqrt(n),
so the chain of Theorem 1(b)/Corollary 2 applied to g* cannot give a rate below Ubar/sqrt(n) for this law.
